## H5: MFA and credential hygiene

```
Hypothesis H5: Administrators authenticate through a central service with MFA, accounts are individual, the built-in admin is not in active use, and lockout and idle timeout are set.

From ADMIN USERS, AUTHENTICATION PROFILES, SERVER PROFILES, PASSWORD COMPLEXITY and MANAGEMENT SETTINGS:

a. Every admin account with ROLE, AUTH-PROFILE and SRC. Count superusers. Is an account literally named "admin" present, and is it bound to an authentication profile or local only?
b. Authentication method (local / radius / tacplus / ldap / saml / kerberos) and the server profile it references.
c. MFA: any factor configured on-box? If the method is RADIUS or SAML, mark MFA NOT-DETERMINABLE and state that enforcement lives on the identity provider.
d. Accounts that look shared or generic (netadmin, service, ops, etc.).
e. admin-lockout failed-attempts and lockout-time, or "lockout disabled" if absent.
f. idle-timeout, or "60-minute default" if absent.
g. password-complexity enabled and minimum-length, or "not enforced" if absent.

Verdict: CONFIRMED only if central auth is in use, no shared accounts, lockout and idle timeout are set, and admin is not local-only. MFA is reported separately as NOT-DETERMINABLE where applicable. Cite rows.
```

