## H6: Panorama enforces uniformly, no weakening overrides

```
Hypothesis H6: All management-plane settings are template-enforced with no local override that weakens them.

a. State the "Sources merged" header line. If TEMPLATE, SP-SHARED or SP-DG is MISSING, say which earlier hypotheses are unreliable as a result.
b. Reproduce APPENDIX A in full. For each DRIFT=yes row, state whether the local value is more or less restrictive than the template value, judging only permitted-ip, service disables, lockout, idle-timeout, and management profile settings. For other objects say "not a management-plane control".
c. For each DRIFT=no row: "locked from Panorama management, identical value" (latent risk: a future template hardening push will not reach it).
d. List every row in SYSTEM, MANAGEMENT SETTINGS, ADMIN USERS and INTERFACE MANAGEMENT PROFILES whose SRC is LOCAL. These are unmanaged by Panorama.

Verdict: CONFIRMED if Appendix A has no weakening drift and no management-plane setting is LOCAL-only. REFUTED otherwise. Cite rows.
```

